// Backward-compatibility read facade for azureVnetLogs (migration step 1 / PR1).
//
// This thin, computationally-cheap view inherits the legacy table name so existing
// readers keep working unchanged while the write path migrates to AllAroHcpLogs.
// It unions the new routed table (tab_azureVnetLogs, fed by the rawLogs update policy) with
// the legacy ServiceLogs.azureVnetLogs table, so the facade returns both new and pre-cutover
// data. During PR1 the forwarder still writes ServiceLogs.azureVnetLogs, so the new side is
// empty until the forwarder is cut over (PR2); legacy data ages out by retention.
//
// union kind=outer tolerates minor column drift between the two sources.
// skipvalidation is required because the cross-database sources are not resolvable
// at script-execution time (validation emulator, single-database deploy).
.create-or-alter function with (view = true, skipvalidation = "true", docstring = "compat view: azureVnetLogs (new tab_azureVnetLogs + legacy ServiceLogs.azureVnetLogs)", folder = "views")
azureVnetLogs() {
    union kind=outer
      database("AllAroHcpLogs").tab_azureVnetLogs,
      database("ServiceLogs").azureVnetLogs
}
